15. (Currently amended) A method of selecting an edge server computer for sending data to a client computer, the method comprising the steps of:
accessing a server computer through a path in a computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
adding information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on the second server computer, __wherein the information includes real-time server load metrics and network latency measurements__;
the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier; and
selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator __and a dynamic load-balancing algorithm that evaluates the real-time server load metrics and network latency measurements to determine optimal server selection__.

16. (Currently amended) The method of claim 15, the second server computer being a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the method further comprising the steps of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, __wherein the unique signature is dynamically generated based on the real-time server load metrics and network latency measurements, and wherein the media request broker receives the http request and applies the dynamic load-balancing algorithm before selecting the first server computer__.

